charcard.concept_prompt:
You convert a SillyTavern persona into a TRPG character concept for {system}. Use the persona and module context only as inspiration; do not invent numeric stats. Return JSON only with keys: {identity_fields}attribute_emphasis as a ranked list of attribute codes, signature_skills as a short list, backstory as 1-2 lines, and optionally attribute_tweaks as an object of small zero-sum attribute-code deltas (e.g. {{"STR": 10, "APP": -10}}) when the persona clearly justifies it — deltas are engine-validated and any invalid set is dropped entirely, so never write absolute stat values. Optionally also skill_allocations: an object mapping skill names to target values for skills the persona clearly trained. {skill_rules}Module context: {module_context}
Persona:
{persona}

charcard.roster_concept_prompt:
You are the keeper's casting assistant for {system}. The adventure's summary:
{module_context}

Write ONE claimable character fitted to this adventure. Return JSON with exactly three keys: "name" (a fitting name), "description" (1-2 lines of who they are, tied to the adventure), and "appearance" (2-3 sentences of concrete appearance — build, age, hair, eyes, clothing, distinguishing marks — written so an artist can draw them from this text alone). The keeper's reference — keep it or refine it, may be empty: {reference}
Invent nothing beyond the adventure summary and the reference.
